<title>BELGIUM: EU backs Dutch, Spanish plans to slaughter 1.8 mln pigs.</title>
<headline>EU backs Dutch, Spanish plans to slaughter 1.8 mln pigs.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union has agreed Dutch and Spanish requests to help finance the slaughter of an extra 1.65 million and 172,000 pigs respectively to combat swine fever, EU Commission officials said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;It's a market support measure,&quot; an official said.</p>
<p>It will bring the total number of animals slaughtered in the two countries to 4.8 million and 362,000 respectively.</p>
<p>In the Netherlands, another 425,000 pigs, 25,000 sows and 1.2 million piglets will be slaughtered. Around 270 cases of swine fever have so far been reported in the national herd of around 12 million pigs.</p>
<p>In Spain, a further 120,000 pigs and 50,000 piglets will be killed.</p>
<p>The EU will finance 70 percent of the cost of slaughtering, the member state financing the balance.</p>
</text>
